  "rejection_before_calls": "The first is a subset regrouping of the already tested square skeleton/tail families, without a new clear geometric misconception. Different upper/lower colors would break the genuine halfturn and change the transformation-count target. A new symmetry-axis line would add geometry to the very figure whose symmetries are counted and risks new explicit condition semantics. No substantively new, simple information-targeted mark set preserving the exact counted figure is credible, so no new PNG or calls.",
  "old_result_caveat": "square_skeleton_symmetry returned1/1 with preset3, a miss; it cannot be relabeled1. tail_orientation_correspondence returned2/1 with preset1, also a miss. Neither is queued.",
  "primary_unique_original_proof": "Upper square centers=(4k+.5,.5), lower=(4k+2.5,-.5). Translation(4,0) and halfturn about(1.5,0) preserve all squares and same-slope diagonal tails. Reflection across ell fails the staggered x locations. Perpendicular reflections would reverse upper-right tail attachment into upper-left, absent. An isometry preserving the infinite horizontal line can have no other nontrivial rotation angle than180 degrees. Exactly2 listed kinds work."
